  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "Travel promotes {understanding} , {expands} our minds, and makes us better people.But the {rapid growth} of travel has led to {overtourism} in certain {regions} and destinations.From ancient {temples} to areas along the {coast} , popular destinations are struggling with the virtual {circus} of crowds.While local {economies} and {communities} benefit from tourist spending in {hotels} , restaurants, and shops, the negative impacts on {civilian} life and cultural heritage are becoming apparent.Many cities are now implementing measures to {prohibit} certain tourist activities and {ban} new tourist shops around {historic} sites.So, should we stop traveling? {Certainly} not.The {loss} of what travel offers would be unacceptable.Here are some tips on making wise decisions to {minimize} pressure on the places we {visit} and improve our experience.",
      "cn": "旅行促进 理解 ， 拓展 我们的思维，使我们成为更好的人。但旅游业的 快速发展 已经导致某些 地区 和旅游目的地出现了 过度旅游 的现象。从古老的 寺庙 到 海滨 地区，热门的旅游目的地都在苦于应对如 马戏团 般喧闹的人群。虽然通过游客在 酒店 、餐馆和商店的消费，当地 经济 和 社区 获得了收益，但旅游业对 平民 生活和文化遗产的负面影响却日益明显。许多城市现在正在采取措施， 叫停 某些旅游活动，并 禁止 在 历史 古迹周围开设新的景区商店。那么，我们是否应该停止旅游呢？ 当然 不是。 失去 旅游带来的种种益处是难以接受的。以下是一些小贴士，教你如何做出明智决策， 最大限度地减少 对我们所 到访 之地的压力，并提升我们的旅游体验。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "Choose mindfully.Over-visited destinations are that way for a reason: they're special.With so many online {posts featuring} the same places, it's easy to feel like you're missing out.Go somewhere only when the landscape, culture, or food deeply draw you.Travel for yourself and no one else.",
      "cn": "慎重选择。那些游客过度聚集的旅游目的地之所以这样是有原因的：它们很特别。网上有大量 帖子 都 以 同样的地方 为主要内容 ，这很容易让人觉得自己错过了这些好地方。只有当风景、文化或美食深深吸引你时，再决定前往某地。旅行只为自己，不为别人。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "Get creative.The best way to ease pressure on over-touristed destinations is to go somewhere else.Though overtourism is described as a problem affecting the entire world, it's actually concentrated in a small number of extremely popular spots.That means you have {tons} of less-visited options instead of {joining} the crowd.You can still find relatively {undiscovered} places.It's advisable to try a {regional} alternative or seek out local {cuisine} in residential {districts} . {Reserving} a room in a local {cottage} rather than a {chain} hotel also offers better cultural immersion.",
      "cn": "发挥创意。要缓解过度旅游目的地所承受的压力，最好的办法就是去别的地方。虽然过度旅游被描述为一个影响全球的问题，但实际上它只集中在少数极受欢迎的景点。这就意味着你还有 大量 游客较少的地方可以选择，而不是 随 大流。你仍然可以找到相对 未被发掘的 去处。建议尝试一个 当地的 其他景点，或是在居民 区 寻找当地 美食 。 预订 当地 村舍 而非 连锁 酒店的房间，也能获得更好的沉浸式文化体验。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "Schedule your travel beyond the typical tourist {circuit} .Maximize your experience by {skipping major} holidays or peak seasons like {July} or {August} .Wisely plan your {departure} time by choosing early morning or evening {hours} , which might be {slightly} less ideal.You'll {compete} with fewer tourists, save money, experience a different side of a popular place, and boost the economy during traditionally slower {tourism} periods.",
      "cn": "将旅行安排在经典的旅游 线路 之外。通过 避开主要 节假日或旺季（如 七月 或 八月 ），来最大限度地提升旅游体验。明智地规划 出发 时间，选择 稍微 不那么理想的时间段，如清晨或夜 间 。如此，与你 竞争 的游客会更少，你可以节省开支，体验到热门景点的另一面，并在传统的 旅游 淡季促进当地经济发展。"
    },
    {
      "num": "05",
      "en": "Visiting a place that others call home is a {privilege} .Do your part to {preserve} what makes a destination special in the first place.Consider giving back to the communities you're visiting.This might mean higher {fees} for attractions, but your effort will benefit both other visitors and local communities in the long run.",
      "cn": "游览一个被他人称之为家乡的地方是一种 荣幸 。尽自己的一份力去 保护 那些让一个旅游胜地首先变得特别的东西。考虑回馈你所游览的社区。这可能意味着景点收 费 变高，但从长远来看，你的努力将使其他游客和当地社区都受益。 5NoOncib/NjiX02BpMIzP4m+378Hw1xTRxUdPaP/PFjKUFq4K2G7tp6ZLYoCE601yW1W39VMdLmovFdSHs4nVQ=="
    }
  ],
